 - **Row 186 (a refusal label is admitted only after its named counterfeits fail it, and at least one arm uses a carrier that no counterfeit's list names).** A frozen refusal label measures a mechanism only if a declared counterfeit set scores `met_target false` under it: a repair that reads the pinned carrier files, a repair that matches the input against a table of pinned packed digests, and a rc-1 exit with no output. The unseen carrier defeats a list-or-table counterfeit only when the counterfeit's list omits it. A list over the full public carrier set still passes (round-92 MutCounter M1, M2; critic CHEAT-D, CHEAT-E): the row is necessary, not sufficient, and a fresh-pack oracle is the remaining fix. Evidence: `.ufo/waves/round-92/pre/c2-do-nothing-v1-counterfeit-{A,B,C}.json` (the round-91 label admits all three); `.ufo/waves/round-92/w1/MutCounter.md` LIM-1, LIM-2.
 
 - **Row 187 (a figure a report states from a census or receipt equals the receipt's own count at the revision the report cites).** A report, lesson or spot-check that quotes a census or receipt count states the value the cited receipt carries, re-derived by the command that reads that receipt. A count taken from another run, or a subset of the true set, is a defect even when the named items are right. Evidence: round-91 D-91-1 (`corpus/lessons/round-91-verifier-spotcheck.md` §5): the report says "7 W04 duplicate-URL warnings"; `.ufo/waves/round-91/l1/census-before.txt` carries 29 W04 lines. Sweep and fixture: `.ufo/waves/round-92/w1/ScribeQuality/sweep-w04.sh`. Correction recorded in `corpus/lessons/round-92.md` (M92-a).
+- **Row 188 (a craft row's criterion citation names a criterion whose text states the rule the row asserts).** A citation that resolves to the right document can still mis-state the rule: craft block 31 row 3 cited QUALITY 169 for the intact-input branch, and row 169 states guard inheritance for superseding instruments — no sentence of it says an intact input must never be refused. Every depth counter that resolved paths stayed green, so the miscite was invisible to the instruments until the round-92 non-author spot-check named it (D-91-3). The semantic atom freezes, per row, the keywords the cited criterion must contain; a wrong citation fails the atom even though the pointer resolves. The fix is a new block (32) whose criterion column cites criteria that state each rule; the misciting block is history, never rewritten. Evidence: before-receipt `.ufo/waves/round-93/pre/r93-c2-block31-before.json` (exit 1, named atom) at base `0a2a23da5eb50410a8a0df90c031d9f4fdadb024`; checker `tools/round-93/craft-citation-semantic.py` (sha256 `34cf6579d7d0614336add1710912877492c68517331736fa5e4021ffedf05340`, `--selftest` 10 cases, 0 failures); lesson `corpus/lessons/round-93.md` (M93-a).
